   "textKind": "explain",
   "content": "**Finland added the most heritage spending per person since before the pandemic, followed by Switzerland.**\n\n| Country | Added per person | Years compared |\n|---|---:|---|\n| Finland | $88.41 | 2019 → 2023 |\n| Switzerland | $55.67 | 2019 → 2022 |\n| Slovakia | $27.76 | 2018 → 2024 |\n| Ecuador | $25.09 | 2019 → 2024 |\n| Canada | $24.59 | 2019 → 2024 |\n\nPublic spending on cultural and natural heritage, adjusted for inflation, among the 31 countries with figures for both periods. Source: UIS, February 2026 release.",
   "parentNodeId": "d_out_2",
   "actionId": "exploreDataFromNL_1792312015543",
